0411AA             0583*    ; inputs: ub.c and ud.e are dx and dy in 16.8 fixed format
0411AA             0584*    ; output: uh.l is the 16.8 fixed format angle in degrees 256
0411AA             0585*    ; destroys: a,hl,bc,de
0411AA             0586*    ; note: only works for angles from 0 to 32 (45) degrees
0411AA             0587*    ;   use atan2_168fast (which calls this proc) to handle the full 256 (360) degrees
0411AA             0588*    atan_168fast:
0411AA             0589*    ; because we use compass headings instead of geometric angles
0411AA             0590*    ; we compute dx/dy which is 1/tan(theta) in the maths world
0411AA             0591*    ; we can do faster unsigned division here because we know dx and dy are positive
       FF FF FF FF 
       FF FF 
